"comparison": "Both BAC and GS disclose the impact of de-designated hedging relationships on the carrying values of debt securities and borrowings. BAC reports that fair value adjustments from de-designated long-term debt and AFS debt securities hedges decreased their respective carrying values by $11.2 billion and $4.4 billion as of December 31, 2024. Similarly, GS reports cumulative hedging adjustments from prior hedging relationships that were de-designated (mostly unsecured long-term borrowings) included in carrying values, amounting to a decrease of $(5.81) billion as of December 2024. Both companies reflect the amortization or inclusion of these adjustments in the carrying value of the associated liabilities/assets after de-designation.",
